From 839171d24266759570f176ed2392ece4ae783cdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:24:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] facilitator-local: finish a settlement whose client
 disconnected; log every broadcast

post_settle awaited the settlement inside the request's future. When the
client disconnected (or a proxy in front of the facilitator timed out), axum
dropped that future, and with it the settlement wherever it was suspended. If
that was after the transaction went out, the transaction was still mined, but
the facilitator forgot it: the pending record's drop guard removed the
authorization's record, nothing logged the hash, and the next /verify of the
same payload went back to the chain instead of naming the pending transaction.

- post_settle runs the settlement on its own task (tokio::spawn, in the
  request's tracing span) and awaits it. A dropped request no longer cancels
  the settlement: it completes, and its outcome is recorded as for any other
  request (the transaction's receipt, or a pending record named by its hash
  when the receipt does not arrive in time). A settlement task that panics is
  answered with 500 unexpected_settle_error.
- The EVM provider logs every broadcast at info level ("Transaction broadcast",
  with the hash, sender and target) before waiting for the receipt, and logs a
  warning with the hash when the receipt does not arrive.

The handler now requires the facilitator state to be Clone + Send + Sync +
'static, as routes() already did.
